what:
Andrew 15:56 bench (cargo signature/generic/newfn off the splice path). In v2, `codegen::link` (codegen.rs:771-798) gives blaze-link every static as removed AND added on every build (`statics: built.statics.iter().collect()`, `removed_statics: std::mem::take(&mut linked.statics)`). blaze-link's `Change` is a delta: `Stage::apply` unmakes each removed static (marking its symbol changed) and `add_static` makes a fresh piece, so every build places every static anew, at a new address, and relocates and rewrites every function that refers to one: close to a full link on every edit (body edits too), and the moved statics eat the reserved room until a stage fails with `... link the image from scratch`. Fix: pass only statics that are new or differ. Exact edit: (1) `Linked.statics` (codegen.rs:563) becomes `Vec<(ItemKey, ContentId, ContentId)>` (item, instance, hash of the whole definition). (2) Replace lines 771-772 with:
    // Each static by what it is and a hash of its definition: one put again unchanged is
    // neither removed nor placed again, which would move it and rewrite every referrer.
    let mut scratch = Vec::new();
    let mut statics: Vec<(ItemKey, ContentId, ContentId)> = Vec::with_capacity(built.statics.len());
    for it in &built.statics {
        scratch.clear();
        blaze_protocol::cbor::append(&mut scratch, it).map_err(|error| format!("the static {:?}: {error}", it.item))?;
        statics.push((it.item, it.instance, ContentId::of("blaze v2 link static 1", &scratch)));
    }
    statics.sort_unstable();
    let (mut gone_statics, mut new_statics) = (Vec::new(), Vec::new());
    diff(&linked.statics, &statics, &mut gone_statics, &mut new_statics);
(3) In the `Change` literal, `statics: built.statics.iter().filter(|it| new_statics.binary_search_by(|n| (n.0, n.1).cmp(&(it.item, it.instance))).is_ok()).collect(),` and `removed_statics: gone_statics.iter().map(|it| (it.0, it.1)).collect(),`, and drop the comment 'A static's value is not in its key: every static is put again.' (4) `linked.statics = statics;` stays. A static whose definition changed is in both lists (old hash gone, new added): removed then made, as now. Relocations name targets by symbol, so an unchanged static whose target function moved is still rewritten by blaze-link's referrer pass. Assumes (item, instance) is unique in `built.statics`. Test: link the same `built` twice into one kept image; the second `Change` has empty `statics` and `removed_statics`, and the second stage writes no static piece (blaze-link `Stage::statics` count 0). blaze-protocol and blaze-ids are already dependencies. Unbuilt; Andrew's 15:21 rule, the coordinator builds.
